       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. CABSXDUP.
      *****************************************************************
      * CABSXDUP - SORT E35 OUTPUT EXIT - SUSPENSE DUPLICATE REMOVAL  *
      * APPLICATION : CABS                                            *
      * COMPILER    : ENTERPRISE COBOL                                *
      * INVOKED BY  : OS SORT/MERGE, MODS E35=(CABSXDUP,16384) ON     *
      *               JCL/CTLCARDS/MVT/CABSRT16                       *
      * INPUTS      : ONE 300 BYTE SUSPENSE RECORD PER ENTRY, FOUR    *
      *               GENERATIONS OF TELCABS.CABS.SUSPENSE MERGED     *
      * OUTPUTS     : ONE RECORD PER DISTINCT SUSPENSE ITEM, THE      *
      *               COPY CARRYING THE OLDEST RUN ID                 *
      * CONTROL     : NONE - EXITS DO NOT WRITE CTLOUT, CABS-STD-041  *
      * BALANCE     : MERGE OUT = SURVIVORS + WS-DUP-DELETED          *
      * RESTART     : NOT RESTARTABLE - RERUN THE WHOLE SORT STEP     *
      *                                                               *
      * LINKAGE CONVENTION                                            *
      *   REGISTER 1 ADDRESSES A THREE WORD PARAMETER LIST.  WORD     *
      *   ONE IS THE ADDRESS OF THE RECORD LEAVING THE FINAL MERGE,   *
      *   OR BINARY ZERO WHEN THE MERGE IS EXHAUSTED.  WORD TWO       *
      *   ADDRESSES THE LAST RECORD WRITTEN AND WORD THREE THE        *
      *   LENGTH HALFWORD.  THE                                       *
      *   REPLY IS PLACED IN RETURN-CODE - 00 TAKE THE NEXT RECORD,   *
      *   04 DELETE, 08 WRITE THE RECORD ADDRESSED BY WORD ONE AND    *
      *   RE-ENTER, 12 NO FURTHER ENTRY, 16 TERMINATE.  AN EXIT THAT  *
      *   PICKS ONE RECORD OUT OF A GROUP MUST HOLD ITS CANDIDATE     *
      *   ACROSS ENTRIES, RELEASE IT AT THE BREAK, THEN REPLY 04 FOR  *
      *   THE RECORD THAT CAUSED THE BREAK ON THE RE-ENTRY.  THAT IS  *
      *   WHY THE BREAK IS HELD IN WS-PENDING-BREAK-SW.  WORKING      *
      *   STORAGE PERSISTS FOR THE LIFE OF THE SORT STEP.             *
      *                                                               *
      * WHAT THIS EXIT DECIDES                                        *
      *   FOUR GENERATIONS OF THE SUSPENSE FILE ARE MERGED FOR THE    *
      *   AGEING REPORT.  A RECORD THAT WAS RECYCLED AND SUSPENDED    *
      *   AGAIN APPEARS ON TWO GENERATIONS WITH THE SAME CONTENT      *
      *  EXCEPT FOR THE RUN ID, SO THE DUPLICATE TEST AS FILED        *
      *   EXCLUDES THE RUN ID FIELD.  THE FIELDS COMPARED ARE THE     *
      *   FOUR SORT KEY FIELDS - 1,4 ERROR CODE, 6,8 DETECTING        *
      *   PROGRAM, 14,30 DETECTING PARAGRAPH AND 56,200 THE ORIGINAL  *
      *   RECORD.  THE SEVERITY BYTE AT 5 IS ALSO OUTSIDE THE         *
      *   COMPARE BECAUSE IT IS DERIVED FROM THE ERROR CODE.  THE     *
      *   RULE WAS CARRIED AS A SUM FIELDS NONE OPERAND ON THE CARD   *
      *   UNTIL THE STEP MOVED TO A SORT WITH NO SUM STATEMENT.       *
      *   THE SURVIVING RECORD IS THE ONE CARRYING THE OLDEST RUN     *
      *   ID.  THE GENERATIONS ARE MERGED OLDEST FIRST AND THIS EXIT  *
      *   ALSO COMPARES THE RUN ID DATE DIRECTLY, SO THE OLDEST RUN   *
      *   ID SURVIVES WHATEVER ORDER EQUAL KEYS ARRIVE IN.  THE       *
      *   AGEING REPORT THEREFORE SEES THE AGE OF THE FIRST           *
      *   SUSPENSION AND NOT THE MOST RECENT ONE.  THAT IS INTENDED   *
      *   AND IS WHY THE OLDEST ITEM LIST IS WORTH LOOKING AT.        *
      *   THE CALLING PROGRAM'S BALANCE IS UNAFFECTED BY THIS         *
      *   MODULE - A SORT STEP WRITES NO CONTROL RECORD OF ITS OWN.   *
      *                                                               *
      * REVISION HISTORY                                              *
      *   V1.00  1990-06-25  R.T.WHEELER   INITIAL - ASSEMBLER F      *
      *   V1.02  1993-11-16  D.OKONKWO     RUN ID OUT OF COMPARE      *
      *   V1.06  1998-09-01  B.R.HALVORSEN FOURTH GENERATION ADDED    *
      *   V2.00  2005-10-11  P.NAIR        RECODED IN COBOL FOR LE    *
      *   V2.02  2011-03-22  T.YAMASHITA   OLDEST RUN ID RETAINED     *
      *   V2.05  2019-05-30  M.HAAS        RECOMPILE ONLY - LE V6.2   *
      *****************************************************************
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER. IBM-370.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER. IBM-370.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01  WS-MODULE-IDENT.
           05  FILLER                  PIC X(08) VALUE 'CABSXDUP'.
           05  FILLER                  PIC X(08) VALUE ' V2.05  '.
       01  WS-SWITCHES.
           05  WS-FIRST-ENTRY-SW       PIC X(01) VALUE 'Y'.
               88  WS-FIRST-ENTRY      VALUE 'Y'.
           05  WS-PENDING-BREAK-SW     PIC X(01) VALUE 'N'.
               88  WS-PENDING-BREAK    VALUE 'Y'.
           05  WS-HOLD-OPEN-SW         PIC X(01) VALUE 'N'.
               88  WS-HOLD-OPEN        VALUE 'Y'.
           05  WS-FINAL-SENT-SW        PIC X(01) VALUE 'N'.
               88  WS-FINAL-SENT       VALUE 'Y'.
       01  WS-COUNTERS.
           05  WS-ENTRY-CNT            PIC S9(11) COMP-3 VALUE 0.
           05  WS-SURVIVOR-CNT         PIC S9(11) COMP-3 VALUE 0.
           05  WS-DUP-DELETED          PIC S9(11) COMP-3 VALUE 0.
           05  WS-HELD-REPLACED        PIC S9(09) COMP-3 VALUE 0.
           05  WS-RUNID-UNREADABLE     PIC S9(09) COMP-3 VALUE 0.
      *
      * THE COMPARE AREA.  THE FOUR SORT KEY FIELDS OF THE HELD
      * RECORD ARE KEPT HERE.  NOTHING ELSE IS PART OF THE TEST.
      *
       01  WS-HELD-KEY.
           05  WS-HK-ERR-CODE          PIC X(04) VALUE SPACES.
           05  WS-HK-DETECT-PGM        PIC X(08) VALUE SPACES.
           05  WS-HK-DETECT-PARA       PIC X(30) VALUE SPACES.
           05  WS-HK-ORIG-RECORD       PIC X(200) VALUE SPACES.
       01  WS-GROUP-WORK.
           05  WS-GW-HELD-STAMP        PIC 9(07) VALUE 0.
           05  WS-GW-THIS-STAMP        PIC 9(07) VALUE 0.
           05  WS-GW-OLDEST-STAMP      PIC 9(07) VALUE 9999999.
      *
      * THE HELD RECORD.  THIS IS THE AREA SORT IS GIVEN AT THE
      * BREAK, SO IT MUST STAY ADDRESSABLE BETWEEN ENTRIES.
      *
       01  WS-HELD-RECORD              PIC X(300).
      *
      * THE RUN ID CARRIES THE CYCLE DATE AS YYDDD IN ITS MIDDLE FIVE
      * BYTES.  IT IS EXPANDED WITH A PIVOT YEAR OF 70 SO A RUN ID
      * FROM THE NINETIES COMPARES BEFORE ONE FROM THE TWO THOUSANDS.
      *
       01  WS-DATE-WORK.
           05  WS-DW-PIVOT-YY          PIC 9(02) VALUE 70.
           05  WS-DW-STAMP-R           PIC 9(07) VALUE 0.
           05  WS-DW-STAMP-RR REDEFINES WS-DW-STAMP-R.
               10  WS-DW-ST-CCYY       PIC 9(04).
               10  WS-DW-ST-DDD        PIC 9(03).
       01  WS-RUN-ID-WORK              PIC X(12) VALUE SPACES.
       01  WS-RUN-ID-R REDEFINES WS-RUN-ID-WORK.
           05  WS-RI-SYSTEM            PIC X(04).
           05  WS-RI-YYDDD             PIC X(05).
           05  WS-RI-SEQ               PIC X(03).
       01  WS-RN-YYDDD                 PIC 9(05) VALUE 0.
       01  WS-RN-R REDEFINES WS-RN-YYDDD.
           05  WS-RN-YY                PIC 9(02).
           05  WS-RN-DDD               PIC 9(03).
      *
       LINKAGE SECTION.
       01  LK-PARM-LIST.
           05  LK-RECORD-PTR           POINTER.
           05  LK-PREV-PTR             POINTER.
           05  LK-LENGTH-PTR           POINTER.
      *
      * A HAND MAINTAINED VIEW OF THE 300 BYTE SUSPENSE RECORD.  THE
      * CARD POSITIONS ARE THE POSITIONS IN THIS VIEW.  THE RUN ID AT
      * 44 IS THE FIELD THE COMPARE LEAVES OUT.
      *
       01  LK-SORT-RECORD.
           05  LK-SU-ERR-CODE          PIC X(04).
           05  LK-SU-ERR-SEVERITY      PIC X(01).
           05  LK-SU-DETECT-PGM        PIC X(08).
           05  LK-SU-DETECT-PARA       PIC X(30).
           05  LK-SU-RUN-ID            PIC X(12).
           05  LK-SU-ORIG-RECORD       PIC X(200).
           05  LK-SU-FILLER            PIC X(45).
      *
       PROCEDURE DIVISION USING LK-PARM-LIST.
       P0000-MAINLINE.
           MOVE ZERO TO RETURN-CODE.
           IF WS-FIRST-ENTRY
               MOVE 'N' TO WS-FIRST-ENTRY-SW
               DISPLAY 'CABSXDUP ENTERED - SUSPENSE CONSOLIDATION'
           END-IF.
           IF LK-RECORD-PTR = NULL
               PERFORM P8000-END-OF-MERGE THRU P8000-EXIT
               GOBACK
           END-IF.
           SET ADDRESS OF LK-SORT-RECORD TO LK-RECORD-PTR.
           IF WS-PENDING-BREAK
               PERFORM P5000-CLEAR-BREAK THRU P5000-EXIT
               GOBACK
           END-IF.
           ADD 1 TO WS-ENTRY-CNT.
           PERFORM P2000-TEST-BREAK THRU P2000-EXIT.
           IF WS-PENDING-BREAK
               GOBACK
           END-IF.
           MOVE 4 TO RETURN-CODE.
           GOBACK.

       P2000-TEST-BREAK.
      * SET THE FOUR KEY FIELDS OF THE INCOMING RECORD AGAINST THE
      * HELD ONES.  ON A MATCH IT IS A DUPLICATE AND IS DELETED AFTER
      * THE RUN ID TEST HAS DECIDED WHICH OF THE TWO IS KEPT.  ON A
      * DIFFERENCE THE HELD RECORD IS RELEASED.
           IF WS-HOLD-OPEN
               CONTINUE
           ELSE
               PERFORM P2600-OPEN-HOLD THRU P2600-EXIT
               GO TO P2000-EXIT
           END-IF.
           IF LK-SU-ERR-CODE = WS-HK-ERR-CODE
              AND LK-SU-DETECT-PGM = WS-HK-DETECT-PGM
              AND LK-SU-DETECT-PARA = WS-HK-DETECT-PARA
              AND LK-SU-ORIG-RECORD = WS-HK-ORIG-RECORD
               PERFORM P3000-ABSORB-DUP THRU P3000-EXIT
               GO TO P2000-EXIT
           END-IF.
           PERFORM P4000-RELEASE-HELD THRU P4000-EXIT.

       P2000-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       P2600-OPEN-HOLD.
      * TAKE A COPY OF THE RECORD AND MAKE IT THE CANDIDATE FOR THIS
      * GROUP.  THE COPY IS WHOLE - THE SEVERITY BYTE AND THE RUN ID
      * TRAVEL WITH IT - WHICH IS WHY THE HELD AREA IS ONE FIELD.
           MOVE LK-SU-ERR-CODE     TO WS-HK-ERR-CODE.
           MOVE LK-SU-DETECT-PGM   TO WS-HK-DETECT-PGM.
           MOVE LK-SU-DETECT-PARA  TO WS-HK-DETECT-PARA.
           MOVE LK-SU-ORIG-RECORD  TO WS-HK-ORIG-RECORD.
           MOVE LK-SORT-RECORD     TO WS-HELD-RECORD.
           MOVE LK-SU-RUN-ID       TO WS-RUN-ID-WORK.
           PERFORM P6000-RUN-STAMP THRU P6000-EXIT.
           MOVE WS-DW-STAMP-R      TO WS-GW-HELD-STAMP.
           MOVE 'Y' TO WS-HOLD-OPEN-SW.

       P2600-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       P3000-ABSORB-DUP.
      * THE INCOMING RECORD IS THE SAME SUSPENSE ITEM ON A DIFFERENT
      * GENERATION AND IS ALWAYS DELETED.  IF ITS RUN ID IS OLDER
      * THAN THE ONE BEING HELD, THE HELD COPY IS REPLACED FIRST SO
      * THAT THE RECORD EVENTUALLY WRITTEN CARRIES THE OLDEST ONE.
           ADD 1 TO WS-DUP-DELETED.
           MOVE LK-SU-RUN-ID TO WS-RUN-ID-WORK.
           PERFORM P6000-RUN-STAMP THRU P6000-EXIT.
           MOVE WS-DW-STAMP-R TO WS-GW-THIS-STAMP.
           IF WS-GW-THIS-STAMP > ZERO
              AND WS-GW-HELD-STAMP > ZERO
              AND WS-GW-THIS-STAMP < WS-GW-HELD-STAMP
               MOVE LK-SORT-RECORD     TO WS-HELD-RECORD
               MOVE WS-GW-THIS-STAMP   TO WS-GW-HELD-STAMP
               ADD 1 TO WS-HELD-REPLACED
           END-IF.
           MOVE 4 TO RETURN-CODE.

       P3000-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       P4000-RELEASE-HELD.
      * HAND THE HELD RECORD TO SORT.  THE RECORD THAT CAUSED THE
      * BREAK IS PRESENTED AGAIN ON THE NEXT ENTRY.
           PERFORM P6400-COUNT-SURVIVOR THRU P6400-EXIT.
           MOVE 'Y' TO WS-PENDING-BREAK-SW.
           MOVE 'N' TO WS-HOLD-OPEN-SW.
           SET LK-RECORD-PTR TO ADDRESS OF WS-HELD-RECORD.
           MOVE 8 TO RETURN-CODE.

       P4000-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       P5000-CLEAR-BREAK.
      * SORT HAS WRITTEN THE HELD RECORD AND IS PRESENTING THE SAME
      * INPUT RECORD AGAIN.  OPEN THE NEW GROUP WITH IT, SUPPRESS IT.
           MOVE 'N' TO WS-PENDING-BREAK-SW.
           PERFORM P2600-OPEN-HOLD THRU P2600-EXIT.
           MOVE 4 TO RETURN-CODE.

       P5000-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       P6000-RUN-STAMP.
      * PULL THE CYCLE DATE OUT OF THE RUN ID AND EXPAND IT TO A
      * SEVEN DIGIT CCYYDDD SO TWO RUN IDS FROM DIFFERENT CENTURIES
      * COMPARE CORRECTLY.  A RUN ID WHOSE DATE POSITIONS ARE NOT
      * NUMERIC LEAVES THE STAMP AT ZERO, IS COUNTED, AND TAKES NO
      * PART IN THE OLDEST RUN ID TEST.
           MOVE ZERO TO WS-DW-STAMP-R.
           IF WS-RI-YYDDD NOT NUMERIC
               ADD 1 TO WS-RUNID-UNREADABLE
               GO TO P6000-EXIT
           END-IF.
           MOVE WS-RI-YYDDD TO WS-RN-YYDDD.
           IF WS-RN-DDD < 1 OR WS-RN-DDD > 366
               ADD 1 TO WS-RUNID-UNREADABLE
               GO TO P6000-EXIT
           END-IF.
           IF WS-RN-YY < WS-DW-PIVOT-YY
               COMPUTE WS-DW-ST-CCYY = 2000 + WS-RN-YY
           ELSE
               COMPUTE WS-DW-ST-CCYY = 1900 + WS-RN-YY
           END-IF.
           MOVE WS-RN-DDD TO WS-DW-ST-DDD.

       P6000-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       P6400-COUNT-SURVIVOR.
      * COUNT THE RECORD ABOUT TO BE WRITTEN AND KEEP THE OLDEST
      * STAMP SEEN - THE HEAD OF THE OLDEST ITEM LIST.
           ADD 1 TO WS-SURVIVOR-CNT.
           IF WS-GW-HELD-STAMP > ZERO
              AND WS-GW-HELD-STAMP < WS-GW-OLDEST-STAMP
               MOVE WS-GW-HELD-STAMP TO WS-GW-OLDEST-STAMP
           END-IF.

       P6400-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       P8000-END-OF-MERGE.
      * RELEASE THE LAST HELD RECORD, THEN REPLY ZERO SO SORT CAN
      * CLOSE SORTOUT.  ONE NOT RELEASED HERE IS NOT WRITTEN AT ALL.
           IF WS-FINAL-SENT
               PERFORM P8600-REPORT THRU P8600-EXIT
               MOVE ZERO TO RETURN-CODE
               GO TO P8000-EXIT
           END-IF.
           IF WS-HOLD-OPEN
               PERFORM P6400-COUNT-SURVIVOR THRU P6400-EXIT
               MOVE 'N' TO WS-HOLD-OPEN-SW
               MOVE 'Y' TO WS-FINAL-SENT-SW
               SET LK-RECORD-PTR TO ADDRESS OF WS-HELD-RECORD
               MOVE 8 TO RETURN-CODE
               GO TO P8000-EXIT
           END-IF.
           MOVE 'Y' TO WS-FINAL-SENT-SW.
           PERFORM P8600-REPORT THRU P8600-EXIT.
           MOVE ZERO TO RETURN-CODE.

       P8000-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       P8600-REPORT.
           DISPLAY 'CABSXDUP ENTRIES     ' WS-ENTRY-CNT.
           DISPLAY 'CABSXDUP SURVIVORS   ' WS-SURVIVOR-CNT.
           DISPLAY 'CABSXDUP DUPS DELETED' WS-DUP-DELETED.
           DISPLAY 'CABSXDUP OLDER FOUND ' WS-HELD-REPLACED.
           DISPLAY 'CABSXDUP RUNID UNUSED' WS-RUNID-UNREADABLE.
           DISPLAY 'CABSXDUP OLDEST STAMP' WS-GW-OLDEST-STAMP.

       P8600-EXIT.
           EXIT.
